.\" Man page for go-flowAPI(1)
.TH GO-FLOWAPI 1 "November 2026" "ETL Madness Flow API" "User Commands and Daemons"
.SH NAME
go-flowAPI \- REST API, artifact repository, live SSE execution gateway, and telemetry daemon for ETL Madness Flow
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B go-flowAPI
.RI [ options ...]
.br
.B go-flowAPI
.B \-hash\-password
.I plaintext
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B go-flowAPI
is the centralized HTTP REST API and background service for the ETL Madness Flow ecosystem.
It embeds the
.B go-flow
pipeline engine and pure-Go database drivers to manage database-stored XML/JSON artifacts
.RB ( pipelines ,
.BR options ,
.BR configs ),
execute and validate pipelines synchronously or over live Server-Sent Events (SSE), provide cryptographic encryption/signing endpoints, enforce database-backed BasicAuth and Active Directory group RBAC, and record full API audit and node execution telemetry across SQL Server, PostgreSQL, MySQL/MariaDB, SQLite, and Oracle.
.PP
On Windows,
.B go-flowAPI.exe
natively implements the Windows Service Control Manager (SCM) dispatcher and runs directly as a Windows Service without third-party service wrappers.
On Linux, FreeBSD, and macOS, packages provide ready-to-enable
.BR systemd (1),
OpenRC, SysVinit, FreeBSD
.BR rc.d (8),
and macOS
.BR launchd (8)
service definitions configured via
.BR go-flow-api.env (5).
.SH OPTIONS
Flags accept single-dash or double-dash Go flag syntax (for example,
.B \-addr
or
.BR \-\-addr ).
Precedence order from lowest to highest: compiled
.IR StartupConnectionString ,
values loaded from
.B \-env\-file
.RB ( FLOW_API_ENV_FILE ),
process environment variables, and explicit command-line flags.
.TP
.BI \-dsn " uri"
Primary startup database connection string override.
Supports
.BR sqlserver:// ,
.BR postgres:// ,
.BR mysql:// ,
.BR sqlite:// ,
and
.BR oracle://
URIs.
Environment variable:
.BR FLOW_API_DSN .
.TP
.BI \-addr " host:port"
HTTP TCP listen address (default
.BR :8080 ).
Environment variables:
.B FLOW_API_ADDR
or
.BR PORT .
.TP
.BI \-env\-file " path"
Path to a
.I KEY=VALUE
environment configuration file loaded before resolving runtime environment variables (see
.BR go-flow-api.env (5)).
Unset variables are populated without overriding variables already present in the process environment.
Environment variable:
.BR FLOW_API_ENV_FILE .
.TP
.BI \-log\-file " path"
Optional file path to append server logs (parent directories are created automatically with mode
.BR 0750 ).
Recommended when running under the Windows Service Control Manager or SysVinit.
Environment variable:
.BR FLOW_API_LOG_FILE .
.TP
.BI \-service\-name " name"
Service name registered with the Windows Service Control Manager when running as a native Windows Service (default
.BR GoFlowAPI ).
.TP
.BI \-secure\-key " passphrase"
Default AES-256-GCM passphrase for encrypting and decrypting protected artifacts.
Environment variables:
.B FLOW_SECURE_KEY
or
.BR SECURE_KEY .
.TP
.BI \-key\-file " path"
Path to a file containing the default encryption/decryption passphrase.
.TP
.BI \-bootstrap\-user " username"
Create or update an initial BasicAuth user in
.I dbo.flow_api_users
at startup.
Environment variable:
.BR FLOW_API_BOOTSTRAP_USER .
.TP
.BI \-bootstrap\-pass " password"
Plaintext password for
.B \-bootstrap\-user
(automatically hashed with bcrypt before storage).
Environment variable:
.BR FLOW_API_BOOTSTRAP_PASS .
.TP
.BI \-bootstrap\-perm " role"
RBAC permission role assigned to
.BR \-bootstrap\-user :
.B all
(default),
.BR execution-only ,
.BR read-only ,
.BR write ,
or
.BR upload .
Environment variable:
.BR FLOW_API_BOOTSTRAP_PERM .
.TP
.BI \-hash\-password " password"
Generate a bcrypt password hash on standard output and exit immediately.
.TP
.B \-debug
Enable verbose request and execution debug logging.
Environment variable:
.B FLOW_API_DEBUG
.RB ( true " or " 1 ).
.SH RBAC PERMISSION ROLES
.TP
.B all
Full administrative access across all endpoints, including user management
.RB ( /api/v1/users ),
database connectivity testing
.RB ( /api/v1/db/test ),
execution, CRUD, and audit logs.
.TP
.B execution-only
Execute and validate pipelines
.RB ( /api/v1/execute ,
.BR /api/v1/execute/stream ,
.BR /api/v1/validate )
plus read-only artifact and telemetry queries.
.TP
.B write " / " upload
Upload XML/JSON files and create, update, delete, and read artifacts
.RB ( /api/v1/upload/* ,
.BR /api/v1/artifacts/* ).
.TP
.B read-only
List, read, and export artifacts and query
.BR /api/v1/runs ,
.BR /api/v1/events ,
and
.BR /api/v1/audit .
.SH OS SERVICE MANAGEMENT
.TP
.B Linux (systemd)
Edit
.I /etc/go-flow-api/go-flow-api.env
and run:
.RS
.nf
sudo systemctl enable --now go-flow-api.service
sudo journalctl -u go-flow-api.service -f
.fi
.RE
.TP
.B Linux (OpenRC)
Install
.I /opt/flow-api/share/services/openrc/go-flow-api
to
.I /etc/init.d/go-flow-api
and run:
.RS
.nf
sudo rc-update add go-flow-api default
sudo rc-service go-flow-api start
.fi
.RE
.TP
.B FreeBSD (rc.d)
Edit
.I /usr/local/etc/go-flow-api/go-flow-api.env
and run:
.RS
.nf
sudo sysrc go_flow_api_enable="YES"
sudo service go_flow_api start
.fi
.RE
.TP
.B macOS (launchd)
Edit
.IR /opt/flow-api/etc/go-flow-api.env ,
copy
.I /opt/flow-api/share/services/launchd/com.etlmadness.go-flow-api.plist
to
.IR /Library/LaunchDaemons/ ,
and run:
.RS
.nf
sudo launchctl bootstrap system /Library/LaunchDaemons/com.etlmadness.go-flow-api.plist
.fi
.RE
.TP
.B Windows (Native SCM Service)
From an elevated PowerShell prompt:
.RS
.nf
& "C:\Program Files\ETL Madness\Flow API\share\services\windows\Install-GoFlowAPIService.ps1" -Start
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /opt/flow-api/bin/go-flowAPI
Installed server binary on Linux, macOS, and FreeBSD.
.TP
.I /etc/go-flow-api/go-flow-api.env
Default daemon environment configuration on Linux.
.TP
.I /usr/local/etc/go-flow-api/go-flow-api.env
Default daemon environment configuration on FreeBSD.
.TP
.I /usr/local/etc/rc.d/go_flow_api
FreeBSD
.BR rc.d (8)
service control script.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/go-flow-api.service
Linux
.BR systemd.service (5)
unit file.
.TP
.I /opt/flow-api/share/sql/*.sql
Database initialization DDL scripts for SQLite, PostgreSQL, and SQL Server.
.SH SIGNALS
.B SIGINT
and
.B SIGTERM
initiate a graceful HTTP shutdown (up to 15 seconds) and record a
.B system.shutdown
audit event before exiting.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR go-flow-api.env (5),
.BR flow (1),
.BR flow-pipeline (5)
